                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "den Freiherren"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "92888162-4c97-40a5-8b4f-9c9ee6135074",
                        "entry_id": "83d76e4e-7989-3bbe-827a-7260d899417a",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Freiherren"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e25fb3cb-0664-36a4-a268-dcf10bf84b70",
                        "entry_id": "83d76e4e-7989-3bbe-827a-7260d899417a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Adelstitel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "no-plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6a7d3db-0f56-42e3-8108-0434a060c46a",
                                "sense_id": "e25fb3cb-0664-36a4-a268-dcf10bf84b70",
                                "text": "Der Adelstitel „Freiherr“ bezeichnet einen Angehörigen des niederen Adels und ist Bestandteil des Familiennamens, er steht nach dem Vornamen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50845da9-d1f5-3949-b076-aacc2f82aa2d",
                        "entry_id": "83d76e4e-7989-3bbe-827a-7260d899417a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Träger dieses Adelstitels"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "033f020a-4d87-411d-9b69-03ed2485939e",
                                "sense_id": "50845da9-d1f5-3949-b076-aacc2f82aa2d",
                                "text": "„Dem Freiherrn selber jedoch war die Popularität als Lügenbaron eher peinlich, zudem erwies sich sein zweifelhafter Ruf bei einem späteren Scheidungsprozess, der ihn finanziell ruinierte, als wenig vorteilhaft.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5193121-40b6-4fe6-a698-8fa6d891e68f",
                                "sense_id": "50845da9-d1f5-3949-b076-aacc2f82aa2d",
                                "text": "„Auch wenn die meisten Gutsherren in den 1930er Jahren keine Grafen und Freiherrn mehr waren, verhielten sie sich oft so.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1a38e561-6861-4723-9ce2-0022e8461797",
                        "source_entry_id": "83d76e4e-7989-3bbe-827a-7260d899417a",
                        "source_sense_id": "e25fb3cb-0664-36a4-a268-dcf10bf84b70",
                        "source_sense_description": "(ohne Plural) Adelstitel",
                        "target_lang_word": "baron",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "baron",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ee56649-2534-3a5b-9ab0-92d1096aec50",
                                        "entry_id": "9c61688d-f2bb-3593-8200-84219ae552dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The male ruler of a barony."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f177b4d-1e95-3510-b377-892a389ceba9",
                                        "entry_id": "9c61688d-f2bb-3593-8200-84219ae552dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male member of the lowest rank of English nobility (the equivalent rank in Scotland is lord)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f112af9-93dd-3736-b3ff-52d88622cb3f",
                                        "entry_id": "9c61688d-f2bb-3593-8200-84219ae552dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person of great power in society, especially in business and politics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f996348a-aff9-4f6f-a108-413df8f8fbe9",
                                                "sense_id": "1f112af9-93dd-3736-b3ff-52d88622cb3f",
                                                "text": "There were a few exotics among them — some South American boys, sons of Argentine beef barons, one or two Russians, and even a Siamese prince, or someone who was described as a prince."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e19bf30c-d8e3-48ec-b07b-b2e0bf04bcbf",
                                                "sense_id": "1f112af9-93dd-3736-b3ff-52d88622cb3f",
                                                "text": "British journalists shun complete respectability, feeling a duty to be ready to savage the mighty, or rummage through their bins. Elsewhere in Europe, government contracts and subsidies ensure that press barons will only defy the mighty so far."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6a92b22-ff81-3b80-969b-b8f3cff4c495",
                                        "entry_id": "9c61688d-f2bb-3593-8200-84219ae552dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prisoner who gains power and influence by lending or selling goods such as tobacco."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c4614e2-2670-4fbf-b52d-c4a66b07cd75",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a92b22-ff81-3b80-969b-b8f3cff4c495",
                                                "text": "The first thing a baron does is to accumulate a supply of tobacco. He spends every penny he can earn on laying it in […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e21d2120-8333-4aa5-894e-c42faabfb6e3",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a92b22-ff81-3b80-969b-b8f3cff4c495",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, from my own agonies of the first few months, after which I did not miss smoking at all, I could appreciate the need of others. It was in this atmosphere of craving that the 'barons' thrived. Barons are prisoners who lend tobacco."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bff0ff14-ed9c-4171-8dce-39f134393b19",
                                                "sense_id": "d6a92b22-ff81-3b80-969b-b8f3cff4c495",
                                                "text": "In British prisons tobacco still remains the gold standard which is made to back every transaction and promise. The official allowance is barely sufficient for individual smoking needs, but tobacco may expensively be borrowed or bought from a baron, possibly through his runner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
